    Bug 1937716 - Port bug 1935714: Build the correct string types for string streams' data in Rust. r=mkmelin

    Bug 1935714 changed the argument type for `Set[ByteString]Data` from a raw char
    pointer to an `nsACString`, so we need to change our call points accordingly.
    Rust strings aren't null-terminated (it uses the pointer + length to determine
    the end of a string), so we need to explicitly call the `nsCString` constructor.

    I've also changed the call points themselves to use the `Deref` trait rather
    than `as_ptr()`, since `nsCString` derefs to an `nsACString`, and `&` can be
    implicitly turned into `*const`.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232329

